From 1f7a3a800773c3bdd01dc1c10f7f581755acbda2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:20:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] Add the WebView2 host and wire the five page entry
 points to it

webview.{h,cpp} is the C++ counterpart of WebLoginWindow.swift and
BilibiliPageWindow.swift: the two JS shims the mini-login page expects, the
cookie store, the COM plumbing and the page automation hooks. It routes every
call to the OBS main thread, which libobs already put in an STA before plugins
load, and it answers honestly when the Evergreen Runtime is missing rather than
opening a window it cannot fill.

CMakeLists picks the static loader by CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR so both the x64 and
arm64 presets link, and the four page entry points plus the two automation
hooks now call into it. open_face_auth_qr still reports a pending state on
purpose: the Swift shows that one in a native window of its own rather than in
a web view, so WebView2 is not what is missing there.

Does not compile yet: MSVC reports ApplyCookieBatch and CookieOperation used in
LoginWindow before the file declares them (webview.cpp:1547-1555). The author
has the exact errors and is fixing them; this commit is the wiring around it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
